<title>USA: Mohave 790 MW unit 1 expected to restart Tuesday.</title>
<headline>Mohave 790 MW unit 1 expected to restart Tuesday.</headline>
<dateline>LOS ANGELES 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The 790 megawatt (MW) unit 1 at the Mohave coal-fired power plant near Laughlin, Nev., is expected to restart early Tuesday after being shut Friday due to a tube leak, sources familiar with the unit said Monday.</p>
<p>Mohave's 790 MW unit 2 was said to be operating normally.</p>
<p>The plant is majority owned and operated by Edison International's Southern California Edison Co.</p>
<p>--D Beasley, Los Angeles bureau + 1 213 955 6761</p>
